        "raw": "<p>I was trying to take the new Termi-Nation heroes for a spin, and I had the game spit me out a random combination of: (1) Captain Cosmic; (2) Parse; (3) Termi-Nation Bunker, and (4) Termi-Nation Unity against the Ennead in Silver Gulch.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Talk about annoying! &nbsp; The Ennead just kept killing off Unity&#39;s bots and CC&#39;s constructs (with the help of the various environment AOE damage cards), while bleeding the other characters dry and making things generally difficult with Ancient Magicks and Mass Overheating. &nbsp; Parse&#39;s deck control doesn&#39;t really work as well against the Ennead because it requires a discard, which just gives them more power usages. &nbsp;And don&#39;t get me started on the number of times you have to hit fast-forward when Elemental Storm comes out, and you have to redirect every single instance of 1 damage away from (ex:) 4 heroes, 5 bots and 3 constructs....</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I&#39;ve replayed it several times, and although I&#39;ve won most of the time, I don&#39;t think I&#39;ve ever had the sort of usual easy victory against the Ennead where all of the heroes are at &gt;20HP. &nbsp;Next step might be to try Advanced or Challenge mode, but with this hero team, that&#39;d be tough. &nbsp;Just thought I&#39;d pass it on for anyone else looking for an interesting challenge.</p>",
